#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Graphics"
msgstr "Grafisme"

#. Tag: primary
#: graphics.docbook:12 graphics.docbook:27 graphics.docbook:186
#: graphics.docbook:193 graphics.docbook:201 graphics.docbook:206
#: graphics.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "graphics"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: graphics.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; is very good at handling textual information. &kword; can also be "
"used to incorporate graphical images with text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A source of great clipart that is free to use is the <ulink url=\"http://www."
"openclipart.org\">Open Clip Art Library</ulink>. This project has a large "
"collection of vector graphics indexed and sorted by category, all released "
"into the public domain."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pictures can be inserted into a document as either <emphasis>framed</"
"emphasis> or <emphasis>inline</emphasis> images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Framed images are pictures that have a frame around them. The frame around a "
"picture functions exactly the same as a frame around text. It contains the "
"picture and determines the size and shape of the picture."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An inline image has a frame around it, but this frame is inserted "
"<emphasis>within</emphasis> the current text frame. If text is inserted in "
"front of the picture, the picture travels down the frame just like any text "
"would. This means the picture will stay in the same area of the page as the "
"text that surrounds it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Framed pictures, on the other hand, need to be moved by hand on the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can use pictures <link linkend=\"insert-graphics\">already stored in "
"a file</link> or <link linkend=\"scan-graphics\"> acquire an image from a "
"scanner</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert Graphics from a file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: graphics.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "inserting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three ways to insert a picture into a document:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Picture...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the keyboard shortcut: <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F5</"
"keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"or by clicking <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"fpicture."
"png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> on the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "All three methods open a file selection dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"file-dialog\">Use this dialog</link> to select the picture."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pressing <keycap>Esc</keycap> at this point will cancel the insertion of a "
"picture into your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the appropriate picture file is located, click on the filename once "
"with the &LMB;. Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to continue."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "A new dialog box appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The right half of this dialog box contains a preview window. The picture "
"should be visible in this window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "The left part of this box contains one button and two check boxes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: graphics.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choose Picture..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this button and &kword; will open a new file dialog to choose a "
"different picture."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: graphics.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert Picture Inline"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is a mark in this check box, the picture will be an inline picture. "
"If there is no mark, a new frame will be created. For details on the "
"differences, see the <link linkend=\"graphics\">introduction</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: graphics.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Retain original aspect ratio"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<glossterm linkend=\"defaspectratio\">Aspect ratio</glossterm> is defined in "
"the &kword; glossary."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a there is a mark in this check box, &kword; will not allow any change "
"the aspect ratio of the picture. This prevents inappropriate stretching and "
"compressing of the image. It will still be possible to change the overall "
"size of the image, but it will not be possible to change the horizontal "
"measurement without also changing the vertical measurement."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is no mark in this check box, the horizontal and vertical sizes of "
"the picture can be changed independently."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To insert the picture, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>. To abort the picture "
"entirely, click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If an inline picture was selected, click with the mouse in the appropriate "
"location. The picture will be inserted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a framed picture was selected, the mouse cursor will change to "
"crosshairs. Locate one corner of the location of the new picture frame with "
"the mouse. Click and hold the &LMB; down. Drag the cursor to adjust the size "
"of the picture frame. When the size of the picture frame is correct, release "
"the &LMB;. &kword; will insert the picture into the frame, and resize the "
"picture to fit within the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a picture from a scanner"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A complete discussion of how to operate a scanner is beyond the scope of "
"this documentation. This document will confine itself to the controls "
"available in &kword; but will not go into detail on the use of these "
"controls."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use a scanner to insert a picture into your kword document, begin by "
"selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Scan Image...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will open a dialog box for you to choose your scanner. Simply click "
"on the radio button to the left of your scanner. Then click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>. This will bring up the scanning dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You should begin by selecting the image type that you want to scan and the "
"resolution. First determine the picture type using the drop down box labeled "
"<guilabel>Scan Mode</guilabel>. You can choose between <guilabel>Color</"
"guilabel>, <guilabel>Greyscale</guilabel> or <guilabel>Binary</guilabel> "
"image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to select a different scanner, click the <guibutton>Source...</"
"guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have selected a <guilabel>Binary</guilabel> image, you can use the "
"drop down box labeled <guilabel>Halftoning</guilabel> to select your "
"halftone protocol."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select your resolution using the drop down box labeled <guilabel>Resolution</"
"guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now place the object you want to scan in the scanner and click "
"<guibutton>Preview Scan</guibutton>. Your scanner will take a low resolution "
"scan and preview it in the window in the far right of the dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using your mouse, click on the upper left corner of he area you want to scan "
"with the &LMB; and hold the button down. Drag the mouse down and to the "
"right to create a box for a high-resolution scan. When you have an "
"appropriate sized box, release the &LMB;. Once the box is drawn, you can "
"adjust the selection box using the mouse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can refer to the box to the left of the preview window labeled "
"<guilabel>Selection</guilabel>. This box will show you the height and width "
"of your selection and the amount of disk space you will need to store this "
"image in the &kword; file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you are satisfied with the size and position of the selection box, "
"click <guibutton>Final Scan</guibutton>. The scanner will scan the selected "
"area at the resolution you selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the scanner is finished, click <guibutton>Close</guibutton> to close "
"the dialog box. Your cursor will now be crosshairs. Using this cursor, draw "
"the size and position you want your picture on the page. The scanned image "
"will be inserted in a separate frame. You can now adjust the size of the "
"picture by <link linkend=\"resize-frame\">changing the size of the frame</"
"link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjusting the image prior to final scanning"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use the lower left part of this dialog to adjust your image prior to "
"scanning."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By moving the slider bar labeled <guilabel>Threshold</guilabel> you can "
"adjust the cutoff point of white in the scanned image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By moving the slider bars labeled <guilabel>Brightness</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Sharpness</guilabel> you can adjust the relative brightness and "
"the sharpness of the scanned image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The preview window will not show you the effects of changes to your scanned "
"image in the preview window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select from one of three pre-defined gamma tables or you can select "
"the <guilabel>User defined</guilabel> option from the drop down box labeled "
"<guilabel>Use custom gamma table</guilabel>. If you selected <guilabel>User "
"defined</guilabel> you can click the <guibutton>Edit...</guibutton> to alter "
"the <guilabel>Brightness</guilabel>, <guilabel>Contrast</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Gamma</guilabel> for your customized gamma table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjusting the preview scan size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you know the size of the object you are scanning, you can select the "
"preview area from the drop-down box labeled <guilabel>Scan size</guilabel>. "
"You can also use the radio buttons labeled <guibutton>Landscape</guibutton> "
"and <guibutton>Portrait</guibutton> to change the orientation of the preview "
"area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changing the orientation between portrait and landscape does not change the "
"orientation of the scanned text or image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using auto-selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; can try to automatically select the object you want to scan. It does "
"this by looking for an area within the preview window that seems to define "
"an object in the picture. By default this option is disabled. You can enable "
"autoselection in this dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The autoselection area of the dialog is located just to the left of the "
"preview window in the middle of the dialog box. It consists of three "
"controls:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: graphics.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Checkbox"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a mark is placed in the checkbox, auto-selection is enabled. If there is "
"no mark in the checkbox, then auto-selection is disabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: graphics.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Drop down box"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This drop down box contains two possible choices: <guilabel>Black</guilabel> "
"and <guilabel>White</guilabel>. If <guilabel>Black</guilabel> is chosen, "
"then &kword; will look for an area surrounded by black to select "
"automatically. If <guilabel>White</guilabel> is chosen, then &kword; will "
"look for an area surrounded by white to select automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: graphics.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Slider bar labeled <guilabel>Threshold</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By adjusting this slider bar, you determine the threshold auto-selection "
"uses to determine the area to select automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Miscellaneous scanning options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two additional options for scanning that are accessed by clicking "
"on the <guilabel>Options</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The checkbox labeled <guilabel>Ask for the scan device on plugin startup</"
"guilabel> toggles the scanner selection dialog on and off. If there is a "
"mark in this checkbox, &kword; will ask you to select your scanner each time "
"you insert a scanned image into your document. If there is no mark, then "
"&kword; uses the previously selected scanner. If you have access to only one "
"scanner, or you only use one scanner, you should remove any mark from this "
"box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The checkbox labeled <guilabel>Query the network for scan devices</guilabel> "
"is also used to select scanners. If there is a mark in this checkbox, "
"&kword; will check your local network for scanners that are available. If "
"there is no mark in this box, &kword; will only look for scanners connected "
"directly to your machine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "To save these options, click <guibutton>Close</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the size of a picture"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: graphics.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "change the size of"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Resizing a picture is done by changing the size of the frame that surrounds "
"it. &kword; will automatically change the picture to fill the entire frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information on changing the size of a frame, see <link linkend=\"resize-"
"frame\">Resizing frames</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "Move Pictures"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: graphics.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "moving"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The only way to move an inline image around on the page, is to alter the "
"flow of the text that surrounds it. If this is causing problems, the picture "
"can always be <link linkend=\"switch-graphics\">changed to a framed picture</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To move a framed picture in &kword; is the same as <link linkend=\"move-frame"
"\">moving any frame</link> in &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete Graphics"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: graphics.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid "deleting"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To delete a graphic in &kword;, simply <link linkend=\"delete-frame\">delete "
"the frame</link> around it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saving Graphic in separate file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: graphics.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "saving in a separate file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can save a picture or graph to a separate file (for use in another "
"document or to archive the graphic)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply click once on the graphic with the &RMB;. A popup menu will appear. "
"Select <guilabel>Save Picture...</guilabel>. A dialog will appear that will "
"allow you to specify where to save the graphic."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This does not remove the picture from the &kword; document file. It is "
"simply a way to extract a picture from a document so it can be archived or "
"used in another application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "Switching between inline and framed pictures"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: graphics.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "switching between inline and framed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Switching between inline pictures and framed pictures is easy in &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change an inline picture to a framed picture"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change in inline picture to a framed picture, click on the desired "
"picture with the &LMB; once. This selects the frame of the picture."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now click and hold with the &RMB; and a popup menu will appear. In this "
"menu, is an item labeled <guilabel>Inline Frame</guilabel>, with a mark in "
"front of it. Select this option by clicking with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "The frame is now an independent and can be moved around freely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: graphics.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change a framed picture to an inline picture"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change a framed picture into an inline picture, click on the desired "
"picture with the &LMB; once. This selects the frame of the picture."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now click and hold with the &RMB; and a popup menu will appear. In this "
"menu, is an item labeled <guilabel>Inline Frame</guilabel>. Select this "
"option by clicking with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; has now converted this to an inline frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: graphics.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; tries to make a reasonable estimation of where in the text the "
"inline image should be inserted."
msgstr ""
